dimensions_checked.result:
Code claims checked against the tree, and they hold:
- siteCSP, New, securityHeaders and render (router.go);
- rawCSP and serveRaw (raw.go);
- pageData and home (home.go);
- adminRaw and adminData (admin.go);
- Latest, PublishedBySlug, OpenRaw and oneReport (reports.go);
- sniffOK accepts the script-bearing reagent;
- the header partial hard-codes next=%2F;
- only home.html renders "header";
- anchorRE accepts any next value;
- newHarness shares st.DB(), so closing the store fails Latest.

One claim is wrong in the letter but harmless: /raw 'reads no identity'. Identify wraps the whole mux (router.go:83) and runs LookupSession for any request with a session cookie, /raw included (session.go:78-79). The response does not depend on it, so the Q-006 and lesson #933 point stands.

Outside claims: nothing found contradicts the headless command-line claims. The Chromium headless_command_handler exists, and a project reports that --virtual-time-budget forces a --headless=new --screenshot capture to finish. Whether that capture includes out-of-process frame pixels is unmeasured, but a 'no' fails loudly. Port matching in frame-ancestors and --ignore-certificate-errors are recalled, each with a loud fallback.

m8: a public /raw lets anonymous readers trigger the Windows replace refusal (ErrBusy). These cases are covered:
- the missing-file 500;
- store-down 503;
- byte-identical 404s across draft, unpublished, deleted, unknown and malformed slugs;
- path variants pinned from observed responses;
- a replace with a stale ETag answering 200.
A report unpublished between the page load and its frame load shows the blocked-frame page, which is cosmetic.

m4 and m5 (CC-001):
- the template rule is quiet on an iframe with no sandbox attribute and on object, embed and frame tags;
- the draft rule misses the gofmt multi-line OpenRaw(…, false,) call;
- the byte-path rule misses http.FileServer(http.Dir) and os.DirFS.
The rules are already appended to fitness.yaml, which is modified in the worktree. Existing rules are unaffected: the headless helper sits under the internal/testutil/** exceptions, and the reagent strings live in a _test.go file.

No new hole in the product path:
- serveRaw is unchanged, with rawCSP's sandbox, script-src 'none', frame-ancestors set to the origin, nosniff and CORP;
- the iframe uses exactly the admin preview's tokens;
- 404s are written before any header, so drafts have no existence oracle;
- allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox is within the constraint, and target=_blank implies noopener.
The only security-adjacent gap is m4: a future template could frame a report unsandboxed, and only the CSP header would remain.

verdicts.why:
The prescribed blank, GET / in the 'No reports yet' state, shoots only the header, the brand, the sign-in anchor and the body background. Everything that renders only beside a found report is missing from it:
- the h1, the date and the permalink;
- the frame border;
- and, decisively, the like count and comments SC-010 and SC-011 put beneath the report.
The case that motivated m1, a heart styled color:red next to the report, appears in W1 but never in this blank. W1 would still read red > 0 as 'a script ran'. The rationale's claim that the blank 'catches the colour from any source, including the like and comment UI SC-010/SC-011 will add' is false.

With a report found, home and readReport pass the same (rep, found). Nothing in the parameters says which page is being drawn, so Next cannot be derived as prescribed. The builder must then do one of three things:
- read r.URL.Path, which is the request and so forbidden by the design;
- send both pages to /reports/<slug>, which changes the decided home-page return to /;
- add an undeclared parameter.
The prescribed `status` is also redundant with `state`: found and empty mean 200, unavailable means 503. A caller can write (200, rep, unavailable) or (503, rep, found). That repeats the 'remembered at each call site' defect m6 was raised to remove. Finally, on a report page with the store down, the lookup failed, so there is no stored slug, and the prescription does not say what Next is then.

verdicts.instead:
Use renderReader(w, r, page, rep, state), with page ∈ {homePage, reportPage} and state ∈ {found, empty, unavailable}. Inside it:
- derive status from state (found and empty give 200, unavailable gives 503);
- derive Title (rep.Title+" - hband" when found, else "hband");
- derive Next: "/reports/"+rep.Slug only for reportPage with found, otherwise "/";
- derive SignedIn and Viewer from auth.ViewerFrom.
The handlers pass no status and no strings.
